Forager patch 0005: residential, unclassified and road streets from zoom 10, so the street grid shows at glance level
as OpenStreetMap's map does (dispatch 2026-10-30-coder-05, after the pilot dispatch 2026-10-30-coder-02).

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2), with 0001 to 0004 already
applied. Applied after them with `git apply` by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

The owner: "Streets only (Recommended)", "Z10 is good, whichever is the one OSM uses", and "From Sunday's run
(Recommended)". OSM Carto draws residential and unclassified from its zoom 12; the app shows OSM's 256 px tiles at
round(map zoom + 1), so from about map zoom 10.5, which only z10 vector tiles can match.

Upstream's minor_road minzoom of 12 becomes FORAGER_STREETS_MIN_ZOOM (10) for residential, unclassified and road, the
way 0001 moved tracks and paths: only the first zoom moves; min_zoom and the sort key keep upstream's values; service
roads, raceways, and private or no-access ways keep upstream's zoom. Line merging and the 0.1 px simplification in
Roads.postProcess are unchanged. Measured (Oregon and New York, the pilot): archives +0.68 % and +0.94 %; largest z10
tile 228,641 bytes (New York), under the 500 KB limit.

Pinned by 7 forager* cases in RoadsTest (foragerStreetsFromZoom10 3, foragerStreetsOthersUnchanged 4), and
upstream's testHighways rows for residential, unclassified and road edited to 10.

